\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {BitMar Architecture.} The model processes multimodal inputs: text tokens and DiNOv2-compressed image features. Quantized encoders (1.58-bit) generate compact text and vision embeddings ($z$, $v$), which are fused via cross-modal attention into shared query representations. A sliding-window attention mechanism enables long-context processing. A fixed episodic memory matrix ($K \times C$) stores and retrieves multimodal context vectors through quantized read/write weights, supporting optional SD-card offloading for edge deployment.}}{22}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bitmar_arch}{{3.1}{22}{}{figure.3.1}{}}
